hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17868","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, he said: 'Adi ibn 'Adi narrated to us, he said: Raja' ibn Haywah and al-'Urs ibn 'Umayrah informed me, from his father 'Adi, he said: A man from Kindah called Imru' al-Qays ibn 'Abis disputed with a man from Hadramawt before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning land, so he ruled against the Hadrami for proof, and he had no proof, so he ruled upon Imru' al-Qays the oath. The Hadrami said: If you enable him to take the oath, O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, or by the Lord of the Ka'bah, my land is gone. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a false oath to cut off thereby the property of his brother will meet Allah while He is angry with him. Raja' said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price. Imru' al-Qays said: What is for one who leaves it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Paradise. He said: Then bear witness that I have left it all for him."
"17869","Twice: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Qays narrated to me, from 'Adi ibn 'Umayrah al-Kindi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, whoever among you performs for us a task and conceals from us of it a needle or more, it is plunder he will bring on the Day of Resurrection. He said: A black man from the Ansar stood, Mujalid said: He is Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, as if I am looking at him, he said: O Messenger of Allah, accept your task from me. He said: And what is that? He said: I heard you say such and such. He said: And I say that now: Whoever we employ upon a task, let him bring its little and its much; what he is given of it he takes, and what he is forbidden he refrains from."
"17870","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Isma'il informed us, from Qays, he said: 'Adi ibn 'Umayrah narrated to me, and he mentioned the hadith."
"17871","Waki' narrated to us: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from 'Adi ibn 'Umayrah al-Kindi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever we employ upon a task, and he mentioned its meaning."
"17872","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Sayf narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Adi ibn 'Adi al-Kindi narrating from Mujahid, he said: A freedman of ours narrated to me that he heard 'Adi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed Allah Almighty does not punish the generality for the deed of the elite until they see the evil among them while they are able to denounce it and do not denounce it; when they do that, Allah punishes the elite and the generality."
"17873","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, he said: 'Adi ibn 'Adi narrated to me, from Raja' ibn Haywah and al-'Urs ibn 'Umayrah, from his father 'Adi, and he mentioned the hadith. Jarir said: And Ayyub added to me, and we were both together when we heard the hadith from 'Adi, he said: 'Adi said: And al-'Urs ibn 'Umayrah narrated to us, and this verse was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, to its end, and I did not memorize it that day from 'Adi."
"17874","Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me, from 'Adi ibn 'Adi al-Kindi, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The previously married woman expresses herself, and the virgin, her consent is her silence."
"17875","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il, he said: I heard Qays narrating from 'Adi ibn 'Umayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever we employ among you upon a task and he conceals from us a needle, it is plunder he will bring on the Day of Resurrection. A tall dark man from the Ansar stood and said: I have no need of your task. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why? He said: I heard you just now say. He said: I say now: Whoever we employ among you upon a task, let him bring its little and its much; if he is given something he takes it, and if he is forbidden he refrains."
"17876","Ali ibn 'Ayyash and Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us, and this is the hadith of Ali, he said: Al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn al-Makki narrated to me, from 'Adi ibn 'Adi al-Kindi, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Consult women concerning themselves. They said: The virgin is shy, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman expresses herself with her tongue, and the virgin, her consent is her silence."
"17877","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Abi Sulayman informed us, he said: I heard 'Adi ibn 'Adi al-Kindi say: A freedman of ours narrated to me that he heard my grandfather say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed Allah Almighty does not punish, and he mentioned the hadith."
"17878","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, he said: Abu Hariz narrated to me that Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated to him that 'Adi ibn 'Umayrah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated, the whiteness of his armpit would be seen, then when he gave salam he would turn with his face to his right until the whiteness of his cheek would be seen, then he would give salam to his left and turn with his face until the whiteness of his cheek would be seen to his left."
"17879","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, and he mentioned the hadith."
